# npm on Windows (`npm.cmd`)

The dev environment is **Windows**. When you suggest or run a command that invokes **npm** in PowerShell or `cmd`, use **`npm.cmd`** instead of the bare string `npm`.

## When

- Scripts documented in responses (`install`, `run`, `exec`, etc.).
- Shell commands for the agent or user in this repo on Windows.

## Examples

```text
✅ npm.cmd install
✅ npm.cmd run build
✅ npx → if invocation issues, prefer `npx.cmd` similarly when relevant.

❌ npm install   (may fail or be ambiguous depending on the shell)
```

On Linux/macOS, `npm` remains the usual form; this rule mainly targets **Windows**.
